rked for it's a pretty sad ending for  a character who never seems to have  things turn out the way he wants despite  their significant age gap  richard burke and monica quickly fall in  love in season two  but soon realize they want totally  different things in life  monica wants to have children of her own  but richard's kids are adults  and he doesn't want any more after some  painful deliberation  the two reluctantly break up several  years later  richard decides that he's willing to  have children if that's what it takes to  be with monica but by then  monica has fallen in love with chandler  who also wants to get married and have  children  accepting that monica already has  everything she wants  richard stops trying to pursue her as  far as we know he never remarries  but eventually winds up selling his  apartment to buy a much larger apartment  with a view of central park  so even if he remains alone he'll be  alone in style  the story of phoebe's teenage  half-brother frank buffet  jr takes a surprising turn when he tells  phoebe that he's fallen in love with his  home economics teacher  alice alice is several decades frank's  senior  but despite their scandalous age gap the  two get married  shortly after tying the knot frank and  alice hurry to have children  using phoebe as a surrogate much to  everyone's surprise phoebe becomes  pregnant with triplets  and frank and alice are thrilled however  in the final season of the show frank  comes to phoebe with an  unusual request i just was thinking that  you know maybe you could take one but  when pressed to pick one  frank realizes he can't bring himself to  part with any of his children  no matter how exhausted he is while  we're glad that frank comes to accept  his role as the father of triplets it's  a little concerning that he's so  overwhelmed  that he comes to the brink of giving  away one of his children  we hope he and alice eventually find a  better balance  gunther is a permanent fixture on  friends although he never gets much of a  story  of his own the one exception is his  long-standing crush  on rachel for most of the series gunther  has strong feelings for her and  experiences significant jealousy towards  the men she dates  occasionally this ventures into creepy  territory  but in the series finale gunther finally  tells rachel  about his feelings i i know you're  you're leaving tonight  but i just have to tell you  i love you even though she doesn't  reciprocate he seems  at peace that makes us hopeful that he's  realized that pining for a woman who  doesn't love him  isn't good for him and that he'll be  content to move on with his life  janice begins as chandler's girlfriend  but she continues popping up  long after their relationship ends in  season 8  janice shows up unexpectedly in the  hospital where rachel is giving birth  revealing that she's also having a baby  with her new  mostly deaf husband sid sid's limited  hearing makes him the perfect match for  janus  whose nasal voice and distinctive laugh  prove off-putting for most other  characters on the show  squeeze your legs together and cover the  baby's ears janice also appears in the  fertility clinic where monica and  chandler are trying to conceive  saying that she insider trying to have  another baby  janice's last appearance is as a  homebuyer who considers purchasing the  home next door to chandler and  monica she decides against it when  chandler pretends to still have feelings  for her  all in all janice seems to have done  pretty well for herself  finding a husband she loves and raising  a family while  always remaining true to herself one of  the most stable relationships throughout  friends is between ross's ex-wife carol  and her partner susan shortly after ross  and carol's son ben  is born following their divorce susan  and carol get married  they have a healthy marriage in which  they keep up a friendly relationship  with ross  the series never gives carol and susan a  definitive  ending but it checks in on them from  time to time mostly in the context of  their shared custody of ben with ross  mostly carol and susan appear to have a  loving and supportive relationship  which only intersects with ross when  they have to share parenting duties  otherwise the couple doesn't seem  wrapped up with carol's x at all  which is probably how it should be one  of the core group of friends  ross's ending well perfect in his own  eyes  comes in at the bottom of the stack  professionally he gets a tenured  position  at new york university he also continues  to share custody of his son with carol  although ben lives with his mom most of  the time on the romantic front  although ross dates many women  throughout the series he consistently  carries feelings for rachel  they have a daughter together emma in  season 8  but don't remain romantically involved  however in the series finale  as rachel prepares to take a job in  paris that would mark a huge step  forward in her career  ross realizes that he's still in love  with her he  asks her to remain in new york with him  and rachel agrees  while ross is overjoyed with her choice  it's hard to overlook that ross's happy  ending comes at the cost of rachel's  career  we can't help but wonder if it ever  crossed ross's mind  to offer to go to paris with rachel  instead of  begging her to give up her job to stay  with him  why do we always have to do everything  according to your  timetable lovable idiot joey tribiani is  the only friend still single by the  show's finale  and of the six main characters he  probably undergoes the least amount of  growth  joey spends years waiting for his big  acting break  which never really comes his biggest  success  is as dr drake ramore on days of our  lives but his character is killed off  only to be brought back to life several  seasons later joey  is nominated for an award for his  performance but never rises beyond that  role  romantically joey tends to avoid serious 